                <pb facs="0917" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.48 Earthquake of 1931/112: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-10T13:00:00-05:45">April 10, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:33 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2. Will Rogers left here this noon by special airplane for San José, Costa Rica.
                    His visit brought cheer to this saddened community and has given new hope to the
                    despondent. He has snapped us out of our morbidness and has given us a saner
                    spirit to carry on our work of reconstruction. We all owe him a profound debt of
                    gratitude.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
